            Slam You In A Sideways Direction With VStats V1.OO

 (-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-)

                             * General Idea *

Nothing fancy, extremely simple - it's just a standard replacement for the
original /X 'S' command except this version looks sexier & gives you more
information than the old one.

 (-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-)

                            * So Why Use It? *

It's written in C so it's faster than all the Rexx replacements available.
It works with /X 3.X [and maybe /X 2.X too, but not tested on it :) ].
It looks prettier than all other stats doors around.
It comes with the TANGo style approval [see IFF screenshot].
It tastes nice [not checked yet....]
Has absolutely NO backdoors!! If you don't belive us then don't install
it [like it bothers us].
Before you install it & regret it, just display the IFF screenshot we've
included for you so you can see if you like the look of it or not before
fucking up your copy of /X. Ahahah. This is a standard feature with ALL
VTools from now on so you can see what you're letting yourself in for
beforehand so there's no excuse....

 (-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-)

                             * Installation *

/X 3.X

Copy the enclosed icon across to BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/
Copy the VStats directory to Doors:
Copy the supplied library to LIBS:
Test it.
Drink copious amounts of alchohol to celebrate the event.

/X 2.X

Make an entry in BBS:Commands/BBSCMD like the following

---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------
*S            RM001DOORS:VStatus/VStatus
---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------

Copy the VStats directory to Doors:
Copy the supplied library to LIBS:
Register for /X 3.X 'cause it's much nicer.

 (-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-·-)

